00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Ji.hlava International Documentary Film Festival (Czech: Mezinárodní festival dokumentárních filmů Ji.hlava), also known as MFDF Ji.hlava or
Ji.hlava IDFF, is a documentary film festival that takes place annually in Jihlava, Czech Republic, typically in late October.

13
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:21,000
The festival was established in 1997 by a group of high school students in Jihlava, led
by Marek Hovorka, who has directed the festival since its inception.

14
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Since 2001, it has been organized by the Jihlava Association of Amateur Filmmakers, which
rebranded as DOC.DREAM - the Association for the Support of Documentary Cinema in 2015.

15
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
Ji.hlava IDFF is a founding member of Doc Alliance, a coalition
of seven European documentary film festivals.

16
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
During the 2022 festival, over 86,000 attendees viewed films, with more than 36,000
attending screenings in cinemas and nearly 50,000 viewing films online.

17
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:21,000
The festival featured 376 films in 2022, and over 1,000 film professionals participated in the Ji.hlava Industry
Programme, which includes initiatives such as Emerging Producers, Festival Identity, and Conference Fascinations.

18
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The 28th edition of the festival was held from 25 October to 3 November 2024, and
the 29th edition took place from 24 October to 2 November 2025.

